=== email subject
[End of life] 2 releases you run are at or near end of life
=== email body
Patchtacio found 2 releases you run at or near the end of security support (endoflife.date). Start with the ones that have already ended.

End of life:
1. [End of life since 30 Sep 2026] Microsoft Windows Server 2016: security updates have stopped
   Security updates for Microsoft Windows Server 2016 stopped on 30 Sep 2026: newly found flaws in it, including ones attackers use, are not fixed any more. Extended support (often paid) is listed until 30 Sep 2029.
   What to do: Upgrade to a supported release. The vendor's lifecycle page says which releases are supported; see https://endoflife.date/windows-server
   Acknowledge with: patchtacio ack eol/microsoft-windows-server/2016
2. [End of life on 30 Nov 2026] Fortinet FortiOS 7.2: security updates stop
   Security updates for Fortinet FortiOS 7.2 stop on 30 Nov 2026, in 58 days. After that, newly found flaws in it, including ones attackers use, will not be fixed.
   What to do: Upgrade to a supported release. The newest supported release listed on endoflife.date is 8.0 (latest version 8.0.1).
   Acknowledge with: patchtacio ack eol/fortinet-fortios/7.2

--
When you have dealt with one, run: patchtacio ack <ID shown>, for example: patchtacio ack eol/microsoft-windows-server/2016
Patchtacio then stops reminding you about it.
You get this alert because Fortinet FortiOS (FortiGate firewalls) and Microsoft Windows Server are on your Patchtacio product list.
